// a mass enchantment covers the whole list in one cast; either way the
// per-stack duration credit saturates at seven.
//
// Three spellings the bytes pin down: the test is `!SpellTargets...`
// (retail materialises the negation with sete before branching, so the
// whole-army arm is the fall-through); the duration product is
// evaluated AFTER that call, which needs the negation parked in its own
// local; and the loop bound is the bare `i < list.size()`, whose
// unsigned comparison is what lets VC6 fold the empty-vector case
// straight to the exit (a `(long)` cast on size() makes it signed and
// costs both the fold and the jae).
